Based on review of hospice policy review, staff interview and clinical record review, the hospice failed to:

1) ensure hospice aides satisfactorily demonstrated competency in the performance of any skills which exceed the level of basic hospice aide skills in the presence of a registered nurse prior to being assigned to perform the task independently (see L0613);

2) ensure the registered nurse provided written hospice aide instructions specific to the needs of each patient (see L0625); and

3) ensure the hospice aide provided services as directed by the hospice aide care plan (see L0626);

The cumulative effects of these systemic practices resulted in the failure of the hospice to ensure hospice aides provided patient care in a manner to meet the individualized needs of all patients effectively and safely.

