Based on review of clinical records and interviews with staff, for one (1) of three (3) patients receiving Aide services (Patient #5), the hospice failed to ensure the Aide Plan of Care (POC) is complete. Failure to ensure the Aide POC is complete and accurate has the potential for the patient to receive inappropriate care.

Patient #5 – This 86-year-old patient with a terminal diagnosis of diastolic heart failure was admitted to the hospice on 10/12/2022.

Review of the Comprehensive Plan of Care dated 10/20/2022 revealed an order for Oxygen 2 L (liters) NC (nasal cannula), PRN (as needed).

Review of the Comprehensive Plan of Care dated 10/27/2022 revealed the following orders:
- Hospice Aide 1x (one time) weekly and 3 PRN visits;
- The hospice Aide is assigned the following tasks:
 - Feed patient as needed every visit;
 - Comb/ brush hair as desired by patient every visit;
 - Shampoo as desired by patient every visit;
 - File nails as needed and tolerated by patient every visit;
 - Oral care assist as desired by patient every visit;
 - Assist with dressing as desired by patient every visit;
 - Change bed linens every visit;
 - Apply lotion as desired by patient every visit;
 - Shower or bed bath every visit; and
 - Toileting, bed pan/ bed side assist every visit.
The Aide Care Plan lacks instructions for 2L PRN Oxygen use and Oxygen precautions to be followed.

