This standard was not met as evidenced by document review and interview that 1 0f 1 (100%) of inpatient units reviewed, the water temperature logs did not follow the required state guidance. 

The state's Administrative Code, 26, Part1, Chapter 554, Sub-chapter D, Division 5, (1) (F) stated: "For design calculation purposes, resident-use hot water must not exceed 110 degrees Fahrenheit at the fixture. For purposes of conforming to licensure requirements, an operating system providing water from 100 degrees Fahrenheit to 115 degrees Fahrenheit is acceptable." 

Water temperature logs for 2022 documented the following:
March 2022 a temperature of 120 degrees, with an adjustment made. There was no documented re-check to assure the temperature adjusted to 115 degrees;
April 2022 a temperature of 118 degrees. There was no documented adjustment to 115 degrees made;
May 2022 a temperature of 118 degrees. There was no documented adjustment to 115 degrees made;
June 2022 a temperature of 118 degrees. There was no documented adjustment to 115 degrees made.

The Safety Coordinator and Director of Clinical Services interviewed on 6/30/2022 validated that the temperatures in 2022 exceeded the required state temperature and did not document an adjustment to the required 115 degrees.

